From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 23:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] signal: count a fault storm by the thread's registers too

The redelivery breaker (ml461, and 0119 for a child) ends a process when
one thread takes the same (pc, address) fault 2,000 times. Rockstar's
RockstarService.exe, started by the Rockstar Games Launcher's installer,
writes one address in its own code on each pass of a loop whose code
shares that 16 KiB host page: each pass takes a self-modifying-code fault
FEX handles, then runs on. It was ended at the 2,000th pass, and the
installer failed with "An error has occurred".

The key now hashes the thread's general registers as well. FEX keeps the
x86 registers in host registers, so a pass that made progress differs;
a resume into the same fault restores the same context and still counts.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-15-rockstar-stage0-phone.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c b/build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c
index 9546afb..5dfff67 100644
--- a/build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c
+++ b/build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c
@@ -7856,6 +7856,18 @@ dispatch:
         static struct { uint64_t key; uint32_t n; } redeliv[16];
         static volatile int ios_redeliv_terminating;
         uint64_t rkey = ((uint64_t)thread << 48) ^ pc ^ ((uint64_t)fault_addr << 1);
+        /* Playport (PLA-275): and the thread's registers. A guest loop that writes the
+         * same address on each pass, with its own code in that host page, takes a
+         * handled self-modifying-code fault at the same (pc, addr) every pass, and
+         * moves on between them: Rockstar's RockstarService.exe did 2,000 passes and
+         * was ended as a storm. FEX keeps the x86 registers in host registers, so a
+         * pass that made progress differs in them; a resume into the same fault (the
+         * storms above) restores the same context and still counts. */
+        {
+            unsigned int ri;
+            for (ri = 0; ri < 29; ri++)
+                rkey ^= state->__x[ri] * (0x9e3779b97f4a7c15ull + 2 * ri);
+        }
         int rslot = (int)((rkey >> 4) & 15);
         if (redeliv[rslot].key != rkey) { redeliv[rslot].key = rkey; redeliv[rslot].n = 1; }
         else if (++redeliv[rslot].n == 256)
